      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_steady_anisotropic_dirichlet",
          "description": "Manufactured steady solution u*(x,y) = sin(pi x) sin(pi y) with c = 1, tensor K = [[1, 1/2], [1/2, 1]] (positive definite). u* vanishes on all four walls of the unit box, so the homogeneous Dirichlet walls (gL=gR=gB=gT=0) are exact and the cell-centered odd-reflection mirror ghost f[0,j]=-f[1,j] reproduces sin's exact odd extension about the wall - the only error is the O(dx^2+dy^2) truncation of the anisotropic operator L, whose cross-derivative half is central_Dxy_dirichlet_bc. Derivation: the continuous balance is u_t = c(L u* + S) = 0 with S = -L u* = 2 pi^2 sin(pi x) sin(pi y) - pi^2 cos(pi x) cos(pi y). With Dirichlet walls the discrete energy estimate's boundary flux vanishes (the test function is zero on the wall), so L is negative definite (dissipative): the field relaxes from u* to a bounded O(dx^2+dy^2) steady offset, the drift the assertions and the convergence sweep measure. The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring; the t=0.1 assertion bounds the truncation drift against the same steady reference. References evaluate at cell centers x_i = (i-1/2)/NX, y_j = (j-1/2)/NY, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and metaparameters only).",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.1
          },
